&lt;h4&gt;About the Job:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Regional Sales Director, you’ll own Enterprise sales performance and strategy within EMEA. You’ll lead a high-performing team of experienced Enterprise Account Executives focused on new business and expansion opportunities, building the pipeline, sales discipline, and customer relationships needed to deliver predictable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll collaborate cross-functionally to drive regional performance and support complex enterprise sales engagements. This role is ideal for a sales leader who understands the developer tools space, is passionate about solving complex customer challenges, and thrives in a high-growth SaaS environment. This role reports to our VP, EMEA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and manage a team of Enterprise Account Executives across EMEA, driving new logo acquisition and expansion within existing enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quarterly and annual team revenue targets, translating regional strategy into clear territory plans and execution priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong outbound pipeline generation culture, partnering with Sales Development and Marketing to create and progress qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional sales forecasting and pipeline inspection, ensuring accurate reporting, clear deal qualification, and proactive management of risks and gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Account Executives through complex sales cycles, including discovery, value articulation, stakeholder engagement, negotiation, and close planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive sponsorship for strategic opportunities and customer relationships, helping the team engage senior technical and business decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leadership and Revenue Operations on annual planning, territory assignments, coverage, capacity, and quota and compensation planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Marketing, Sales Development, Revenue Operations, and Enablement to improve sales execution and deliver a coordinated customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, onboard, develop, and retain high-performing sales talent, fostering an inclusive culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of enterprise SaaS software sales experience, including 5+ years in enterprise sales management, or equivalent depth of experience and demonstrated impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of meeting or exceeding team revenue targets and leading experienced sales teams across complex enterprise sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading sales teams across EMEA markets and adapting territory and account strategies to regional customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build pipeline, deliver accurate forecasts, and coach teams to improve deal qualification, progression, and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and developing sales teams, including hiring, onboarding, performance management, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to technical buyers and engaging senior engineering, technology, and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MEDDPICC and Command of the Message, or comparable sales methodologies, and the ability to apply them consistently through coaching and deal inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional management, interpersonal, written, and presentation skills, with strong cross-functional collaboration and business judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how software delivery platforms improve engineering productivity, release velocity, and delivery confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
