&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4826&quot; data-local-id=&quot;b322305c9cc5&quot;&gt;LaunchDarkly is building the&lt;a href=&quot;https://launchdarkly.com/platform/agent-control/?utm_source=zoom&amp;amp;utm_medium=redirect&amp;amp;utm_campaign=general_zoom_redirect&quot;&gt; runtime control layer for the AI era&lt;/a&gt;, helping engineering teams govern what ships in production and how software and AI agents behave after deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4826&quot; data-local-id=&quot;b322305c9cc5&quot;&gt;As Senior Accounting Manager, you’ll play a key role in strengthening the financial operations behind that work: owning critical close and technical accounting activities, supporting international entities and audit readiness, and partnering across Finance, Technology, and the business. You’ll also lead and develop a global team while improving accounting workflows, systems, and controls, including through automation and AI. This is an opportunity to combine hands-on accounting expertise with meaningful leadership and operational impact at a company shaping how teams build and run software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing global accounting team with clear roles, decision rights, objectives, and development plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and accelerate close activities for key corporate accounting functions, including general accounting, treasury, accounts payable, employee reimbursements, and corporate card program management, and identify opportunities for close timeline compression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, and variance analyses in compliance with US GAAP and internal accounting policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute technical accounting for stock-based compensation (ASC 718), leases (ASC 842), and foreign currency matters (ASC 830), including drafting analyses and memos for review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the implementation of a procure-to-pay (PTP) tool, with a focus on the PO-to-Pay workflow, partnering with Procurement, IT, and business stakeholders from requirements through rollout and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and partner with the International Accounting team to ensure intercompany transactions and subsidiaries’ financial reporting are accurate and timely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technology teams and business stakeholders on ERP enhancements/implementations, integrations, and reporting improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and maintain accounting policies, procedures, and key controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement opportunities for workflow improvement and systems optimization/AI automation across the close and accounting operations lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in accounting, finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least eight years of progressive accounting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years of experience leading a team of accountants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of US GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in NetSuite (or a similar ERP), including improving workflows and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently with strong accountability and initiative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience using automation and AI tools to improve efficiency and accuracy in accounting operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a multi-entity, multi-currency environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work across Finance and the business and explain complex accounting clearly to leaders, auditors, and colleagues outside Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
